# N4 (LMX_semantics.ru.md #method-parts: fn, fm and sub keep the separate contract of their declarations; plan D10):
# the fn h that S defines is a place of the code. Passed as a callable actual of the type of f, h is read from the
# code -- never from the data at the same position, where D keeps its pad -- and app runs it: x gets 3. Entry 7.
fn: f () int
    return: 1
end: f
fn: app (f: g) int
    return: g()
end: app
S:
    fn: h () int
        return: 3
    end: h
    int: x app(h)
end: S
D:
    int: pad 5
    int: x 0
end: D
call: S D
int: r 81
if: D\x = 3 && D\pad = 5
    r: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
